  "file_path": "/home/myuser/playbooks/juce-vst-business-trial2/research/best-practices.md",
  "content": "# Best Practices & Standards: VST Plugin Development

## JUCE Framework Best Practices (2025-2026)

### Build System: CMake Over Projucer

| Aspect | CMake (Recommended) | Projucer |
|--------|---------------------|----------|
| Version control | Excellent (text-based) | Poor (GUI-generated) |
| CI/CD integration | Native support | Difficult |
| Cross-platform | Automatic | Manual regeneration |
| IDE support | Better (IntelliSense) | Limited |

**Best Practice:** Use CMake with FetchContent for self-contained builds.

```cmake
cmake_minimum_required(VERSION 3.22)
project(MyPlugin)

include(FetchContent)
FetchContent_Declare(JUCE
    GIT_REPOSITORY https://github.com/juce-framework/JUCE.git
    GIT_TAG juce-8.0.4)

set(CMAKE_CXX_STANDARD 17)
add_subdirectory(${JUCE_SOURCE_DIR})
```

### C++ Standard: C++17 or C++20

Modern JUCE projects should use **C++17 minimum** (C++20 preferred):

- `constexpr` and compile-time optimizations
- Structured bindings
- RAII patterns for resource management
- `std::atomic` with proper memory ordering

### Thread-Safe Parameter Management

```cpp
namespace Parameters {
    inline const juce::ParameterID gainParam{"gain", 1};

    inline juce::AudioProcessorValueTreeState::ParameterLayout createLayout() {
        std::vector<std::unique_ptr<juce::RangedAudioParameter>> params;

        params.push_back(std::make_unique<juce::AudioParameterFloat>(
            gainParam, "Gain",
            juce::NormalisableRange<float>(0.0f, 1.0f, 0.01f),
            0.5f));

        return {params.begin(), params.end()};
    }
}
```

### Real-Time Audio Safety

**Never on Audio Thread:**
- `new`/`delete` — use pre-allocation
- `std::mutex::lock()` — use lock-free structures
- `malloc()`/`free()` — use memory pools
- File I/O — use background threads
- System calls — avoid entirely
- Virtual function first calls — warm up in prepareToPlay()

**Best Pattern:**
```cpp
void prepareToPlay(double sampleRate, int samplesPerBlock) override {
    // ✅ Pre-allocate all buffers
    workBuffer.setSize(2, samplesPerBlock);

    // ✅ Initialize DSP state
    filter.prepare({sampleRate, (juce::uint32)samplesPerBlock, 2});
    filter.reset();

    // ✅ Warm up virtual calls
    filter.processSample(0.0f);
}
```

### Memory Ordering

Use `acquire/release` for efficient one-way data transfer:

```cpp
// UI Thread
void updateGain(float newGain) {
    gain.store(newGain, std::memory_order_release);
}

// Audio Thread
float processAudio() {
    return gain.load(std::memory_order_acquire);
}
```

### Plugin Distribution Locations

| Platform | User Location | System Location |
|----------|---------------|-----------------|
| Linux VST3 | `~/.vst3/` | `/usr/lib/vst3/` |
| macOS VST3 | `~/Library/Audio/Plug-Ins/VST3/` | `/Library/Audio/Plug-Ins/VST3/` |
| macOS AU | `~/Library/Audio/Plug-Ins/Components/` | `/Library/Audio/Plug-Ins/Components/` |
| Windows VST3 | — | `C:\Program Files\Common Files\VST3\` |

## DSP Implementation Standards

### Testing Framework (Catch2)

```cpp
#include <catch2/catch_test_macros.hpp>
#include "FilterCore.h"

TEST_CASE("FilterCore processes audio correctly", "[dsp]") {
    FilterCore filter;
    filter.reset();
    filter.setFrequency(1000.0f, 44100.0f);

    // Impulse response test
    float impulse[128] = {1.0f};
    float output[128];

    for (int i = 0; i < 128; ++i)
        output[i] = filter.processSample(impulse[i]);

    REQUIRE(output[0] != 0.0f);
    REQUIRE(std::abs(output[127]) < 0.01f);
}
```

### Validation Tools

- **pluginval** — Official JUCE plugin validator
- **AddressSanitizer** — Memory safety
- **ThreadSanitizer** — Thread safety
- **Strict warnings** — `-Wall -Wextra -Wpedantic`

## Sound Design Standards

### Synthesis Type Taxonomy

| Type | Core Mechanism | Best For |
|------|---------------|----------|
| **Subtractive** | Rich oscillators + filters | Classic analog sounds |
| **FM** | Operator modulation | Bells, metallic, electric pianos |
| **Wavetable** | Morphing between waveforms | Evolving pads, modern basses |
| **Granular** | Grain manipulation | Textures, atmospheres |
| **Additive** | Harmonic summing | Organ-like, precise control |

### Parameter Smoothing

All modulation must be smoothed to prevent clicks:

```cpp
juce::SmoothedValue<float> smoothedCutoff;

void prepareToPlay(double sr, int) {
    smoothedCutoff.reset(sr, 0.02f); // 20ms smoothing
}

void processBlock(juce::AudioBuffer<float>& buffer, juce::MidiBuffer&) {
    for (int channel = 0; channel < buffer.getNumChannels(); ++channel) {
        for (int sample = 0; sample < buffer.getNumSamples(); ++sample) {
            float cutoff = smoothedCutoff.getNextValue();
            // Use smoothed value
        }
    }
}
```

## UI/UX Standards

### Control Selection

| Control Type | Best For | Considerations |
|--------------|----------|---------------|
| **Knobs** | Space-efficient, familiar | Awkward mouse interaction |
| **Sliders** | Level comparison, intuitive | Limited by length resolution |
| **Gauges** | Hybrid benefits | Requires user learning |

### Accessibility Requirements

- Minimum 44x44px touch targets
- Full keyboard support (arrows, Page Up/Down, Home/End)
- ARIA labels for screen readers
- High-contrast mode support

### Visual Standards

- Dark theme dominant in audio software
- Group related controls logically
- Visual hierarchy through spacing
- Clear feedback on interaction

## Commercial Distribution Standards

### Licensing Options

| Solution | Type | Cost | Complexity |
|----------|------|------|------------|
| **iLok Cloud** | Industry standard | Revenue share | Medium |
| **Machine Activation** | Offline-friendly | Revenue share | Medium |
| **MuseHub DRM** | SDK-based | Revenue share | Low |
| **Custom** | Full control | Development time | High |

### Marketing Timeline

| Phase | Days Before Launch | Activities |
|-------|-------------------|------------|
| Foundation | 30-23 | Landing page, email capture, social accounts |
| Community | 22-16 | Content publishing, forum engagement |
| Amplification | 15-9 | Guest posts, podcasts, private beta |
| Launch Prep | 8-1 | Final messaging, content scheduling |

### Pricing Strategy

- Consider free "LE" version for list building
- Indie plugins typically $19-$99 range
- Bundle strategies for multiple products

## Sources

- [JUCE Official Course](https://juce.com/learn/course/)
- [Audio Developer Conference](https://conference.audio.dev/)
- [Using locks in real-time audio processing](https://timur.audio/using-locks-in-real-time-audio-processing-safely)
- [Memory ordering for audio](https://www.bruce.audio/post/2025/02/24/memory_ordering/)
- [Synthesizer sound design techniques](https://blog.landr.com/types-of-synthesis)
- [Ambient and drone VST plugins](https://artistsindsp.com/the-11-best-vst-plugins-for-ambient-and-drone-music-in-2025/)"
